    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build passes. Here's a summary.\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, touching **4 files**:\n\n1. **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now assigns the `memberId`: `REGION` (`Locality`) + `FY` (2-digit fiscal year) + `HASH8` (the existing SHA-256-over-`telephone+lastName` first-8-upper-hex) + `CHK` (Luhn check digit over the base). It stores the value in the existing `customerCode` slot, so downstream deduplication needed no change \u2014 **collision handling now applies to the memberId automatically**.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 dropped the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings; added a single `memberId` mapping. `fiscalYear` still maps as before.\n\n3. **`SaveOwner.java`** \u2014 the **audit record** (both the log line and the structured event) now references `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` schema properties; added one `memberId` property (regenerates the `OwnerDto` at build time).\n\n## Design choices for low structural impact\n\n- **Reused the check-digit logic unchanged**: `CheckDigit.of(owner)` already computes Luhn over the digits of whatever is in `customerCode`, so I set the base first, then append `CheckDigit.of(owner)` \u2014 no edit to `CheckDigit`.\n- **Left the `Owner` entity untouched** (it's a large class) by repurposing its `customerCode` storage slot to hold the `memberId`, which also meant **`DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode` needed no change**.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` passes (memberId starts with `NSW`, contains the HASH8, old fields gone).\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS` (the whole project, including the regenerated DTO + MapStruct mapper, compiles). Sample audit output confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
